# A machine with no identity vault still practises, and says why it is unsealed.
#
# "Sealing is not a gate" is the doctrine; this is its receipt. The page must
# not simply omit the persona line when there is no vault, because a blank
# where an identity claim belongs reads as "sealed" to anyone not looking hard.
#
# Drive under a LOCALAPPDATA whose `personae/vault` cannot be created (a file
# in the way), which is how the no-vault branch is forced on a machine that
# has one.

log persona line: no vault, still practising, and it says so
settle 3

click .pill Settings
settle 2

assert text Not sealed
assert text saved in the clear
capture 01_settings_persona_unsealed

log unsealed receipt complete
